# CODEOWNERS
#
# Reflects the support-tier policy in SUPPORT.md: core + the Malanta
# provider are officially owned and reviewed by maintainers; generic-adapter
# VENDOR CONFIGS (docs/providers.md examples) are intentionally NOT owned
# here — they're community/best-effort, and requiring a maintainer review
# for every vendor config would recreate the support burden this
# architecture is designed to avoid.
#
# Order matters: later patterns override earlier ones.

# Default: unowned (no required reviewer) unless a more specific rule below
# applies.
*

# Core packages: the verdict cascade, extraction, cache, config, hookrunner,
# and the hook binaries themselves.
/internal/verdict/          @malanta-ai/trustgate-maintainers
/internal/extract/          @malanta-ai/trustgate-maintainers
/internal/cache/            @malanta-ai/trustgate-maintainers
/internal/config/           @malanta-ai/trustgate-maintainers
/internal/hookrunner/       @malanta-ai/trustgate-maintainers
/cmd/                       @malanta-ai/trustgate-maintainers

# The reputation package: owns both the Malanta provider AND the generic
# adapter ENGINE (the code, not vendor config data — those live in
# docs/providers.md and are intentionally excluded above by the wildcard).
/internal/reputation/       @malanta-ai/trustgate-maintainers

# Security-sensitive governance files always need maintainer eyes.
/SECURITY.md                @malanta-ai/trustgate-maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @malanta-ai/trustgate-maintainers
